  "id": "investment-model",
  "term": "investment model",
  "definition": "In developmental research, the investment model refers to the idea that a family’s economic resources affect children’s development by being turned into investments in the child’s life. These investments can be material, such as educational spending and learning materials, or relational, such as supportive parent–child interactions.",
